                                                              "summary":  "Damodaran examines the 2026 resurgence of the rate-versus-equity debate as US Treasury yields climbed from 4.18% to 4.75% year-to-date. Despite this headwind, equity markets held firm because surging corporate earnings growth more than offset the higher discount rates applied to future cash flows. He walks through sector-level performance ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â energy leading, consumer stocks lagging ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â and extends the analysis globally, noting that rate rises are widespread but their equity impact varies sharply by region and business type. His core finding is that the traditional \u0027higher rates hurt stocks\u0027 rule is not universal and depends heavily on whether earnings growth can absorb the valuation compression.",
